    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0849" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/1715</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Téllez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-16">April 16, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Supreme Court of Justice of
                    New York has ordered to be delivered to the Consulate General of Mexico in that
                    city two documents, on several sheets, relative to a certain suit brought in
                    that court by <hi rendition="#italic">Gustavo Gallopin</hi> vs. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thomas W. Lament, and others, <pb facs="0850" n="730"
                            xml:id="pg730"/> and the United Mexican States;</hi> which documents
                    have been forwarded to me here.</p>
                <p>As my Government is that of a sovereign country and therefore does not recognize
                    the jurisdiction or competence of any foreign court in affairs concerning the
                    Nation, I take the liberty of enclosing herewith to Your Excellency the two
                    documents above mentioned,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d782-f1"/> with the request
                    that, if you see fit, you will have the kindness to order their return to the
                    competent authority, in order that it [i. e. the foregoing]<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d782-f2"/> may thus be made a matter of record.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to thank Your Excellency in advance for the favor and to renew
                    to you the assurances, etc., etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel C. Téllez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
